## Compatibility change

- Added fourteen Java 5.5.1 heartbeat DTO input cases for uppercase numeric
  suffixes, exponent and decimal-point forms, lowercase suffix rejection, and
  numeric suffix coercion to a string field.
- The Rust normalizer now handles `L`, `F`, `D`, `B`, and `S` suffixes,
  leading-dot and trailing-dot decimals, and Java Float/Double string forms.
  The 1,102-case Rust heartbeat DTO differential and focused numeric formatter
  regression pass.
- This closes the observed token and string-field cases only. Broader Fastjson
  grammar and P18-V01 source/API/settings/input/error/control-flow/reverse-
  export reconciliation remain open.

